    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/github_import_migration/SKILL.md"
    end_line: 59
    content: "---\nname: \"github-import-migration\"\ndescription: >-\n  Execute-First migration for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio.\n  Triages projects and routes to the appropriate self-contained migration\n  reference. Supports Web (Node.js) and Android (Kotlin/Compose) runtimes.\n---\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nAttempt the simplest possible refactoring to make the app boot in AI Studio.\n\nFor every blocker: Strip if non-essential \342\206\222 Mock with in-memory stubs if\nboot-critical \342\206\222 Rewrite to the nearest supported paradigm only as last resort.\n\n## Scope Restrictions\n\n-   Do NOT restyle the application (no Tailwind migration, no design changes)\n-   Do NOT add new features or libraries that did not exist in the original\n-   Focus ONLY on making the existing code run in this environment\n-   Preserve the app\'s existing functionality as closely as possible\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Project Triage\n\nRead the full project structure. Classify into ONE category below, then read the\nindicated reference file. **STOP reading this file after routing.**\n\n### Category A: Native Android\n\nIF `build.gradle` or `build.gradle.kts` exists at root or in `app/`, AND the\nproject contains `.kt` or `.java` source files under `app/src/`:\n\n\342\206\222 Read `references/android.md` and follow its instructions. **STOP here.**\n\n### Category B: Cross-Platform Mobile (Unsupported)\n\nIF ANY of: `pubspec.yaml`, `react-native`/`expo` in deps,\n`@capacitor/core`/`@ionic/*` in deps, iOS-only (`*.xcodeproj` without\n`build.gradle`), KMP (`shared/` + `composeApp/` or `androidApp/`):\n\n\342\206\222 These cannot run directly. Create a NEW web app (Vite+React or Next.js)\nreplicating the core 3-5 features. Use `references/web.md` constraints.\n\n### Category C: Web / Node.js Compatible\n\nIF `package.json` exists, OR the project uses a convertible server-side language\n(Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java/Spring, C#, Rust, Elixir):\n\n\342\206\222 Read `references/web.md` and follow its instructions. **STOP here.**\n\n### Category D: Unsupported / Exotic\n\nC/C++, Jupyter notebooks, desktop apps (Electron/Qt/Tkinter), game engines\n(Unity/Unreal/Godot), data/ML pipelines with no UI:\n\n\342\206\222 Create a NEW web app replicating core logic. Use `references/web.md`\nconstraints. Explain to user what was built and what was left out.\n"
    raw_content: "---\nname: \"github-import-migration\"\ndescription: >-\n  Execute-First migration for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio.\n  Triages projects and routes to the appropriate self-contained migration\n  reference. Supports Web (Node.js) and Android (Kotlin/Compose) runtimes.\n---\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nAttempt the simplest possible refactoring to make the app boot in AI Studio.\n\nFor every blocker: Strip if non-essential \342\206\222 Mock with in-memory stubs if\nboot-critical \342\206\222 Rewrite to the nearest supported paradigm only as last resort.\n\n## Scope Restrictions\n\n-   Do NOT restyle the application (no Tailwind migration, no design changes)\n-   Do NOT add new features or libraries that did not exist in the original\n-   Focus ONLY on making the existing code run in this environment\n-   Preserve the app\'s existing functionality as closely as possible\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Project Triage\n\nRead the full project structure. Classify into ONE category below, then read the\nindicated reference file. **STOP reading this file after routing.**\n\n### Category A: Native Android\n\nIF `build.gradle` or `build.gradle.kts` exists at root or in `app/`, AND the\nproject contains `.kt` or `.java` source files under `app/src/`:\n\n\342\206\222 Read `references/android.md` and follow its instructions. **STOP here.**\n\n### Category B: Cross-Platform Mobile (Unsupported)\n\nIF ANY of: `pubspec.yaml`, `react-native`/`expo` in deps,\n`@capacitor/core`/`@ionic/*` in deps, iOS-only (`*.xcodeproj` without\n`build.gradle`), KMP (`shared/` + `composeApp/` or `androidApp/`):\n\n\342\206\222 These cannot run directly. Create a NEW web app (Vite+React or Next.js)\nreplicating the core 3-5 features. Use `references/web.md` constraints.\n\n### Category C: Web / Node.js Compatible\n\nIF `package.json` exists, OR the project uses a convertible server-side language\n(Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java/Spring, C#, Rust, Elixir):\n\n\342\206\222 Read `references/web.md` and follow its instructions. **STOP here.**\n\n### Category D: Unsupported / Exotic\n\nC/C++, Jupyter notebooks, desktop apps (Electron/Qt/Tkinter), game engines\n(Unity/Unreal/Godot), data/ML pipelines with no UI:\n\n\342\206\222 Create a NEW web app replicating core logic. Use `references/web.md`\nconstraints. Explain to user what was built and what was left out.\n"
    num_lines: 60
    num_bytes: 2312
  }
}
