    content: "# Web Migration (Node.js Runtime) \342\200\224 Self-Contained\n\nThis file contains ALL instructions for migrating web projects to AI Studio.\nRead top-to-bottom. Do NOT navigate to other reference files.\n\n## AI Studio Web Constraints\n\n- **Runtime**: Node.js 22, npm only. No yarn, pnpm, bun.\n- **Port**: 3000 is the ONLY accessible port. Host must be `0.0.0.0`.\n- **Entry**: `npm run dev` must start the app on port 3000.\n- **Filesystem**: Ephemeral \342\200\224 container sleeps \342\206\222 disk wiped.\n- **Networking**: HTTP(S) outbound only. Direct TCP to external databases is\n  blocked. Exception: Cloud SQL uses Unix Domain Sockets.\n- **Container**: linux-x64 (Node.js 22-slim). No native compilation tools.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: Project Normalization\n\n### 1.1 Package Manager\n\n- DELETE: `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`,\n  `.yarnrc.yml`, `.yarnrc`, `.pnpmfile.cjs`\n- DELETE: `.DS_Store` files (recursive) \342\200\224 macOS metadata, must not be committed\n- KEEP: `package-lock.json` (if present)\n- Remove `\"packageManager\"` field from package.json\n- Remove `\"preinstall\": \"npx only-allow ...\"` scripts\n- Resolve `catalog:` version specifiers to real versions\n- Convert `\"resolutions\"` \342\206\222 `\"overrides\"` (npm format):\n  `\"resolutions\": { \"webpack/terser\": \"5.31.0\" }` \342\206\222\n  `\"overrides\": { \"webpack\": { \"terser\": \"5.31.0\" } }`\n- Rewrite ALL `yarn`/`pnpm`/`bun` commands in scripts, Makefile, Procfile:\n  `yarn <script>` \342\206\222 `npm run <script>`, `pnpm exec` \342\206\222 `npx`, `bunx` \342\206\222 `npx`\n- If `install_applet_dependencies` fails with peer conflicts \342\206\222\n  `shell_exec npm install --legacy-peer-deps`\n\n### 1.2 Node Version\n\n- DELETE: `.nvmrc`, `.node-version`\n- If `engines.node` excludes 22: update or remove\n\n### 1.3 Monorepo Detection\n\nIF `turbo.json`, `nx.json`, `lerna.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or\n`\"workspaces\"` in package.json, OR `apps/`/`packages/` with own package.json:\n\n1. Keep workspace structure intact. Do NOT flatten.\n2. Pick the most deployable app (priority: Next.js > Vite/React > Express > any with `dev` script)\n3. Ensure root package.json has `\"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\", \"packages/*\"]`\n4. Delete `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Map `\"workspace:*\"` \342\206\222 `\"*\"` in deps.\n5. Wire root dev script: `\"dev\": \"npm run dev --workspace=apps/<chosen>\"`\n6. Keep `turbo.json`/`nx.json` if present (they work with npm)\n\n### 1.4 Deno / Bun Runtime\n\nIF `deno.json`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, or source contains `Deno.serve`,\n`Bun.serve`, URL imports:\n\n**Delete**: `deno.json`, `deno.jsonc`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`\n\n**Create/update package.json** with `\"type\": \"module\"` and dev script.\n\n**Convert ALL runtime APIs using this table:**\n\n| Deno/Bun API | Node.js Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `Deno.serve(handler)` | `express()` + `app.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')` |\n| `Deno.readTextFile(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path, \'utf-8\')` |\n| `Deno.writeTextFile(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Deno.env.get(\"KEY\")` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Deno.openKv()` | In-memory `new Map()` |\n| `Bun.serve({ port, fetch })` | `express()` + route handler |\n| `Bun.file(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path)` |\n| `Bun.write(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Bun.env.KEY` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Bun.password.hash(pw)` | `bcryptjs.hash(pw, 10)` \342\200\224 install `bcryptjs` |\n| `Bun.password.verify(pw, hash)` | `bcryptjs.compare(pw, hash)` |\n| `Bun.hash(data)` | `crypto.createHash(\'sha256\').update(data).digest()` |\n| `Bun.sleep(ms)` | `new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms))` |\n| `Bun.Glob` | `glob` npm package |\n\n**Convert frameworks:**\n\n| Source Framework | Convert To |\n|---|---|\n| Oak (Deno) | Koa (NOT Express \342\200\224 Oak is a Koa clone) |\n| Fresh (Deno) | Next.js |\n| Elysia (Bun) | Fastify |\n| Hono | Keep Hono \342\200\224 add `@hono/node-server` |\n\nIf project uses TypeScript without a build step, add `tsx`:\n`install_applet_package([\"tsx\"], isDevDependency=true)` and\n`\"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"`\n\n### 1.5 Non-Node.js Languages\n\nIF primary runtime is Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java, or other (no package.json):\n\n1. Analyze: catalog endpoints, models, templates, auth, env vars\n2. Pick target framework:\n   - Pure API \342\206\222 Express or Fastify\n   - Fullstack with \342\211\2455 templates \342\206\222 Express + EJS\n   - Fullstack with <5 templates \342\206\222 Next.js\n3. Rewrite core 3-5 routes with in-memory data (`Map`/`Array`, NOT real ORMs)\n4. Stub remaining routes with `res.status(501).json({ error: \'Not yet migrated\' })`\n5. Use language conversion tables below for syntax mapping\n6. **CRITICAL CLEANUP**: After successfully creating and compiling the Node.js app, you MUST delete the original source files and configs (e.g., `.py`, `.go`, `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, `compose.yml`, `alembic/`) to avoid polluting the repository and confusing build rules. Keep only `README.md` and `LICENSE`.\n\n**Python \342\206\222 Node.js**: `@app.route` \342\206\222 `router.get`, `request.json` \342\206\222 `req.body`,\n`request.args.get` \342\206\222 `req.query`, `jsonify(data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`,\n`Blueprint` \342\206\222 `express.Router()`, `Depends()` \342\206\222 Fastify hooks\n\n**Django/Rails/Laravel \342\206\222 Express+EJS**: Models \342\206\222 in-memory Map/Array,\n`{% extends %}` \342\206\222 `<%- include(\'header\') %>`, `@foreach` \342\206\222 `<% for() { %>`\n\n**Go \342\206\222 Node.js**: `c.JSON(200, data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`, `c.Param(\"id\")` \342\206\222\n`req.params.id`, goroutines \342\206\222 synchronous inline\n\n### 1.6 Infrastructure Artifacts\n\n- Do NOT delete Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, fly.toml \342\200\224 scan for env vars\n- Extract env vars into `.env.example`\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: Dependencies\n\n### 2.1 Native Addons\n\n| Package | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `sharp`, `esbuild`, `@swc/core`, `re2`, `@node-rs/*`, `fsevents` | KEEP |\n| `bcrypt` | SWAP \342\206\222 `bcryptjs` |\n| `argon2` | SWAP \342\206\222 `@node-rs/argon2` |\n| `node-sass` | SWAP \342\206\222 `sass` |\n| `canvas`, `puppeteer` | STRIP + comment out imports |\n| `cpu-features`, `microtime` | STRIP |\n\nFor unlisted native addons: try `install_applet_dependencies` first. If\n`node-gyp` / `gyp ERR!` / `make: not found` \342\206\222 STRIP and comment out imports.\n\n### 2.2 Database & Data Layer \342\200\224 MOCK IMMEDIATELY\n\nScan deps for: `pg`, `postgres`, `mysql2`, `mongoose`, `mongodb`, `redis`,\n`ioredis`, `better-sqlite3`, `prisma`, `drizzle-orm`, `typeorm`, `sequelize`,\n`knex`, `bull`, `bullmq`, `kafkajs`, `amqplib`.\n\n**IF ANY found \342\206\222 apply the matching mock template NOW:**\n\n#### Redis / KV (`redis`, `ioredis`)\nReplace the redis import/client creation with:\n```javascript\n// MOCKED \342\200\224 in-memory, data lost on container sleep\nconst store = new Map();\nexport const redis = {\n  get: async (k) => store.get(k) ?? null,\n  set: async (k, v) => { store.set(k, v); return \'OK\'; },\n  del: async (k) => store.delete(k),\n  incr: async (k) => { const n = (store.get(k) || 0) + 1; store.set(k, n); return n; },\n};\n```\n\n#### Mongoose / MongoDB (`mongoose`, `mongodb`)\nFind the file calling `mongoose.connect()`. Wrap in try-catch:\n```javascript\nimport mongoose from \'mongoose\';\nmongoose.set(\'bufferCommands\', false); // CRITICAL: fail fast, don\'t hang\nmongoose.connect(process.env.MONGODB_URI || \'mongodb://localhost/mock\')\n  .catch(err => console.warn(\'MongoDB not connected \342\200\224 some features may not work\'));\n\n// CRITICAL route-level fallback: Add Express error middleware in app.js/server.js\n// to handle database queries failing gracefully when MongoDB is offline:\napp.use((err, req, res, next) => {\n  if (err.name === \'MongooseError\' || err.name === \'MongoNetworkError\' || err.message.includes(\'buffering timed out\')) {\n    console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database offline \342\200\224 returning mock empty response\');\n    if (req.method === \'GET\') {\n      // Return empty array/object depending on route path suffix pluralization\n      return res.json(req.path.endsWith(\'s\') || req.path.endsWith(\'s/\') ? [] : {});\n    }\n    return res.status(503).json({ error: \'Service temporarily unavailable (database offline)\' });\n  }\n  next(err);\n});\n```\n\n#### Drizzle ORM (`drizzle-orm`)\nFind the file calling `drizzle()`. Wrap the entire export:\n```typescript\nlet db;\ntry {\n  db = drizzle(/* original connection */);\n} catch {\n  console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database not connected \342\200\224 using mock\');\n  const noOp = { findMany: async () => [], findFirst: async () => null,\n    findUnique: async () => null, create: async (d) => d?.data ?? {},\n    update: async (d) => d?.data ?? {}, delete: async () => ({}) };\n  db = new Proxy({}, {\n    get: (_, prop) => prop === \'query\'\n      ? new Proxy({}, { get: () => noOp }) : async () => [],\n  });\n}\nexport { db };\n```\n\n#### Prisma (`prisma`, `@prisma/client`)\nFind the PrismaClient initialization. Wrap it:\n```typescript\nlet prisma;\ntry {\n  prisma = new PrismaClient();\n} catch {\n  console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database not connected \342\200\224 using mock\');\n  const noOp = { findMany: async () => [], findFirst: async () => null,\n    findUnique: async () => null, create: async (d) => d?.data ?? {},\n    update: async (d) => d?.data ?? {}, delete: async () => ({}) };\n  prisma = new Proxy({}, { get: () => noOp });\n}\nexport { prisma };\n```\n\n#### PostgreSQL / MySQL raw (`pg`, `postgres`, `mysql2`)\n```javascript\nlet db;\ntry { db = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL }); }\ncatch { console.warn(\'DB not connected \342\200\224 mock active\');\n  db = { query: async () => ({ rows: [] }), connect: async () =>\n    ({ query: async () => ({ rows: [] }), release: () => {} }) }; }\nexport { db };\n```\n\n#### Background Jobs (`bull`, `bullmq`, `kafkajs`, `amqplib`)\nRewrite `queue.add(\'job\', data)` \342\206\222 call the handler function directly inline.\nRemove queue/worker setup. Keep handler functions.\n\n#### SQLite (`sqlite3`, `better-sqlite3`)\nSTRIP native package. Replace with mock:\n```javascript\nexport const db = { prepare: () => ({ get: () => null, all: () => [],\n  run: () => ({ changes: 0 }) }) };\n```\n\n### 2.3 Platform SDKs\n\nScan deps for `@vercel/*`, `@netlify/*`, `@cloudflare/*`:\n\n| Package | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `@vercel/analytics`, `@vercel/speed-insights`, `@vercel/og` | STRIP: remove from deps, replace component with `() => null` |\n| `@netlify/functions`, `@netlify/plugin-*` | STRIP |\n| `@cloudflare/workers-types`, `netlify-identity-widget` | STRIP |\n| `@vercel/kv`, `@vercel/blob`, `@vercel/postgres` | MOCK: replace with in-memory Map stub |\n| `@netlify/blobs` | MOCK: replace with in-memory Map |\n| `@cloudflare/kv-asset-handler` | MOCK: replace with static file serving |\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: Framework Configuration\n\nClassify by deps (first match wins), then apply fixes inline:\n\n### Next.js (`next` in deps)\n- Dev script: `\"dev\": \"next dev -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0\"`\n- Add `output: \'standalone\'` to `next.config.js/ts/mjs`\n- If custom `server.js` exists with `createServer()`: remove it\n  (`standalone` is incompatible with custom servers)\n- Remove `export const runtime = \'edge\'` from any route/middleware\n- Remove Vercel/Cloudflare image loaders from `next/image` config\n\n### Nuxt (`nuxt` in deps)\n- Config: `nitro: { preset: \'node-server\' }`, `devServer: { port: 3000, host: \'0.0.0.0\' }`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"nuxt dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### SvelteKit (`@sveltejs/kit` in deps)\n- SWAP adapter: remove `@sveltejs/adapter-vercel` etc \342\206\222\n  install `@sveltejs/adapter-node`\n- Update `svelte.config.js`: `import adapter from \'@sveltejs/adapter-node\'`\n- **CRITICAL import fix**: search ALL `.svelte` and `.ts` files for\n  `from \'@sveltejs/adapter-vercel\'` and delete those imports \342\200\224 they are\n  type-only adapter config exports that don\'t exist in adapter-node\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vite dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Remix (`@remix-run/*` in deps)\n- Remove `@remix-run/cloudflare`, `@remix-run/vercel`, `@remix-run/deno`\n- Keep/install `@remix-run/node`\n- **CRITICAL import fix**: Replace ALL `from \"@remix-run/cloudflare\"` \342\206\222\n  `from \"@remix-run/node\"` in EVERY route file (`app/routes/`, `app/root.tsx`).\n  Every route typically has this import. Missing even one crashes the build.\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"remix vite:dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Astro (`astro` in deps)\n- SWAP adapter: remove `@astrojs/vercel` etc \342\206\222 install `@astrojs/node`\n- Config: `output: \'server\'`, `adapter: node({ mode: \'standalone\' })`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"astro dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### React SPA (Vite) \342\200\224 `react` in deps, no `next`\n- Vite config: `server: { host: \'0.0.0.0\', port: 3000, allowedHosts: \'all\' }`\n- Or dev script: `\"dev\": \"vite --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### React SPA (CRA) \342\200\224 `react-scripts` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"PORT=3000 HOST=0.0.0.0 react-scripts start\"`\n\n### Angular \342\200\224 `@angular/core` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"ng serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n- If SSR (`@angular/ssr`): ensure `server.ts` binds to `0.0.0.0:3000`\n\n### Vue (plain, no Nuxt) \342\200\224 `vue` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vite --port 3000 --host 0.0.0.0\"`\n\n### SolidStart \342\200\224 `solid-start` in deps\n- Config: `server: { preset: \'node-server\' }`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vinxi dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Gatsby \342\200\224 `gatsby` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"gatsby develop -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0\"`\n\n### Node.js Backend Only (Express/Fastify/NestJS/Koa/Hono, no frontend)\n- Rewrite `.listen()` to: `.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')`\n- NestJS: `await app.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')`\n- Fastify: `listen({ port: 3000, host: \'0.0.0.0\' })`\n- Hono: `serve({ fetch: app.fetch, port: 3000, hostname: \'0.0.0.0\' })`\n- If entry is TypeScript: add `tsx` and `\"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"`\n- WebSockets on separate port: multiplex over 3000:\n  `const wsServer = new WebSocket.Server({ server: httpServer })`\n\n### SPA + Backend (both frontend and backend in same repo, not monorepo)\nAI Studio runs ONE process via `npm run dev`. Do NOT use `concurrently`.\n- **Preferred**: Build frontend, serve from backend:\n  `\"dev\": \"npm run build:frontend && node server.js\"` + add\n  `app.use(express.static(\'client/dist\'))` AFTER API routes + SPA fallback\n- **Alternative** (if backend has <10 routes): merge API into frontend framework\n\n### Static Site (just HTML, no framework)\n- Find `index.html` in root, `public/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `docs/`\n- Create `server.js` with Express serving the static dir on port 3000\n- `\"dev\": \"node server.js\"`, add `express` to deps\n\n### Unrecognized\n- Try as-is: ensure `dev` script starts on port 3000 (host `0.0.0.0`)\n- Run `install_applet_dependencies` \342\206\222 `compile_applet`\n- Rewrite to supported framework only as last resort\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: Integration Wiring\n\n### Gemini SDK\nIF `@google/generative-ai` or `@google/genai` is in dependencies:\n- Swap `@google/generative-ai` \342\206\222 `@google/genai`\n- Ensure API calls are server-side ONLY\n- Remove hardcoded API keys\n- Add `GEMINI_API_KEY=` to `.env.example`\n\n### Firebase\n- Extract Firebase API key to `.env.example` (FIREBASE_API_KEY=)\n- Ensure no hardcoded production credentials in `initializeApp()` config\n- If `firebase-applet-config.json` exists, use as-is\n\n### Third-party LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)\n- Ensure API calls are server-side ONLY\n- Add API key variable names to `.env.example`\n\n### Secrets & Env Scan\n1. Scan all source files for `process.env.*` and `import.meta.env.*`\n2. Scan existing .env, .env.local, .env.development for key names\n3. Generate or merge into `.env.example`\n\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\n### Chunked Execution\n\nExecute in discrete chunks. After each phase, yield a status message:\n\n```\n\"\342\234\205 Phase 1 complete. Changes made:\n- Converted from pnpm to npm\n- Detected monorepo \342\200\224 wired root dev script to apps/web (Next.js)\nMoving to dependency validation...\"\n```\n\n### Verification Loop\n\n1. Run `install_applet_dependencies` then `compile_applet`\n2. If errors \342\206\222 read the error, fix the specific issue, retry\n3. Repeat up to 3 times\n\n### Circuit Breaker (HARD STOP)\n\nIf `compile_applet` fails 3 times and you cannot resolve the error: STOP.\nExplain the specific error to the user and ask for help.\n\n### Post-Execution Summary\n\nAfter successful compilation (or circuit breaker), output:\n\n```\n\"\342\234\205 Migration complete! Here\'s what I changed:\n\n**Runtime**: Web (Node.js)\n**Framework**: Detected [framework]\n**Package Manager**: Converted from [original] to npm\n**Dependencies**:\n- [list each mocked/stripped/swapped dependency and why]\n**Config**: [framework-specific changes]\n**Port**: Dev server on port 3000 (0.0.0.0)\n\nTo connect a real database, provision AI Studio Cloud SQL from the\nintegrations menu.\"\n```\n"
    raw_content: "# Web Migration (Node.js Runtime) \342\200\224 Self-Contained\n\nThis file contains ALL instructions for migrating web projects to AI Studio.\nRead top-to-bottom. Do NOT navigate to other reference files.\n\n## AI Studio Web Constraints\n\n- **Runtime**: Node.js 22, npm only. No yarn, pnpm, bun.\n- **Port**: 3000 is the ONLY accessible port. Host must be `0.0.0.0`.\n- **Entry**: `npm run dev` must start the app on port 3000.\n- **Filesystem**: Ephemeral \342\200\224 container sleeps \342\206\222 disk wiped.\n- **Networking**: HTTP(S) outbound only. Direct TCP to external databases is\n  blocked. Exception: Cloud SQL uses Unix Domain Sockets.\n- **Container**: linux-x64 (Node.js 22-slim). No native compilation tools.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: Project Normalization\n\n### 1.1 Package Manager\n\n- DELETE: `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`,\n  `.yarnrc.yml`, `.yarnrc`, `.pnpmfile.cjs`\n- DELETE: `.DS_Store` files (recursive) \342\200\224 macOS metadata, must not be committed\n- KEEP: `package-lock.json` (if present)\n- Remove `\"packageManager\"` field from package.json\n- Remove `\"preinstall\": \"npx only-allow ...\"` scripts\n- Resolve `catalog:` version specifiers to real versions\n- Convert `\"resolutions\"` \342\206\222 `\"overrides\"` (npm format):\n  `\"resolutions\": { \"webpack/terser\": \"5.31.0\" }` \342\206\222\n  `\"overrides\": { \"webpack\": { \"terser\": \"5.31.0\" } }`\n- Rewrite ALL `yarn`/`pnpm`/`bun` commands in scripts, Makefile, Procfile:\n  `yarn <script>` \342\206\222 `npm run <script>`, `pnpm exec` \342\206\222 `npx`, `bunx` \342\206\222 `npx`\n- If `install_applet_dependencies` fails with peer conflicts \342\206\222\n  `shell_exec npm install --legacy-peer-deps`\n\n### 1.2 Node Version\n\n- DELETE: `.nvmrc`, `.node-version`\n- If `engines.node` excludes 22: update or remove\n\n### 1.3 Monorepo Detection\n\nIF `turbo.json`, `nx.json`, `lerna.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or\n`\"workspaces\"` in package.json, OR `apps/`/`packages/` with own package.json:\n\n1. Keep workspace structure intact. Do NOT flatten.\n2. Pick the most deployable app (priority: Next.js > Vite/React > Express > any with `dev` script)\n3. Ensure root package.json has `\"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\", \"packages/*\"]`\n4. Delete `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Map `\"workspace:*\"` \342\206\222 `\"*\"` in deps.\n5. Wire root dev script: `\"dev\": \"npm run dev --workspace=apps/<chosen>\"`\n6. Keep `turbo.json`/`nx.json` if present (they work with npm)\n\n### 1.4 Deno / Bun Runtime\n\nIF `deno.json`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, or source contains `Deno.serve`,\n`Bun.serve`, URL imports:\n\n**Delete**: `deno.json`, `deno.jsonc`, `bunfig.toml`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`\n\n**Create/update package.json** with `\"type\": \"module\"` and dev script.\n\n**Convert ALL runtime APIs using this table:**\n\n| Deno/Bun API | Node.js Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `Deno.serve(handler)` | `express()` + `app.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')` |\n| `Deno.readTextFile(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path, \'utf-8\')` |\n| `Deno.writeTextFile(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Deno.env.get(\"KEY\")` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Deno.openKv()` | In-memory `new Map()` |\n| `Bun.serve({ port, fetch })` | `express()` + route handler |\n| `Bun.file(path)` | `fs.promises.readFile(path)` |\n| `Bun.write(path, data)` | `fs.promises.writeFile(path, data)` |\n| `Bun.env.KEY` | `process.env.KEY` |\n| `Bun.password.hash(pw)` | `bcryptjs.hash(pw, 10)` \342\200\224 install `bcryptjs` |\n| `Bun.password.verify(pw, hash)` | `bcryptjs.compare(pw, hash)` |\n| `Bun.hash(data)` | `crypto.createHash(\'sha256\').update(data).digest()` |\n| `Bun.sleep(ms)` | `new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms))` |\n| `Bun.Glob` | `glob` npm package |\n\n**Convert frameworks:**\n\n| Source Framework | Convert To |\n|---|---|\n| Oak (Deno) | Koa (NOT Express \342\200\224 Oak is a Koa clone) |\n| Fresh (Deno) | Next.js |\n| Elysia (Bun) | Fastify |\n| Hono | Keep Hono \342\200\224 add `@hono/node-server` |\n\nIf project uses TypeScript without a build step, add `tsx`:\n`install_applet_package([\"tsx\"], isDevDependency=true)` and\n`\"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"`\n\n### 1.5 Non-Node.js Languages\n\nIF primary runtime is Python, Go, Ruby, PHP, Java, or other (no package.json):\n\n1. Analyze: catalog endpoints, models, templates, auth, env vars\n2. Pick target framework:\n   - Pure API \342\206\222 Express or Fastify\n   - Fullstack with \342\211\2455 templates \342\206\222 Express + EJS\n   - Fullstack with <5 templates \342\206\222 Next.js\n3. Rewrite core 3-5 routes with in-memory data (`Map`/`Array`, NOT real ORMs)\n4. Stub remaining routes with `res.status(501).json({ error: \'Not yet migrated\' })`\n5. Use language conversion tables below for syntax mapping\n6. **CRITICAL CLEANUP**: After successfully creating and compiling the Node.js app, you MUST delete the original source files and configs (e.g., `.py`, `.go`, `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, `compose.yml`, `alembic/`) to avoid polluting the repository and confusing build rules. Keep only `README.md` and `LICENSE`.\n\n**Python \342\206\222 Node.js**: `@app.route` \342\206\222 `router.get`, `request.json` \342\206\222 `req.body`,\n`request.args.get` \342\206\222 `req.query`, `jsonify(data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`,\n`Blueprint` \342\206\222 `express.Router()`, `Depends()` \342\206\222 Fastify hooks\n\n**Django/Rails/Laravel \342\206\222 Express+EJS**: Models \342\206\222 in-memory Map/Array,\n`{% extends %}` \342\206\222 `<%- include(\'header\') %>`, `@foreach` \342\206\222 `<% for() { %>`\n\n**Go \342\206\222 Node.js**: `c.JSON(200, data)` \342\206\222 `res.json(data)`, `c.Param(\"id\")` \342\206\222\n`req.params.id`, goroutines \342\206\222 synchronous inline\n\n### 1.6 Infrastructure Artifacts\n\n- Do NOT delete Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, fly.toml \342\200\224 scan for env vars\n- Extract env vars into `.env.example`\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: Dependencies\n\n### 2.1 Native Addons\n\n| Package | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `sharp`, `esbuild`, `@swc/core`, `re2`, `@node-rs/*`, `fsevents` | KEEP |\n| `bcrypt` | SWAP \342\206\222 `bcryptjs` |\n| `argon2` | SWAP \342\206\222 `@node-rs/argon2` |\n| `node-sass` | SWAP \342\206\222 `sass` |\n| `canvas`, `puppeteer` | STRIP + comment out imports |\n| `cpu-features`, `microtime` | STRIP |\n\nFor unlisted native addons: try `install_applet_dependencies` first. If\n`node-gyp` / `gyp ERR!` / `make: not found` \342\206\222 STRIP and comment out imports.\n\n### 2.2 Database & Data Layer \342\200\224 MOCK IMMEDIATELY\n\nScan deps for: `pg`, `postgres`, `mysql2`, `mongoose`, `mongodb`, `redis`,\n`ioredis`, `better-sqlite3`, `prisma`, `drizzle-orm`, `typeorm`, `sequelize`,\n`knex`, `bull`, `bullmq`, `kafkajs`, `amqplib`.\n\n**IF ANY found \342\206\222 apply the matching mock template NOW:**\n\n#### Redis / KV (`redis`, `ioredis`)\nReplace the redis import/client creation with:\n```javascript\n// MOCKED \342\200\224 in-memory, data lost on container sleep\nconst store = new Map();\nexport const redis = {\n  get: async (k) => store.get(k) ?? null,\n  set: async (k, v) => { store.set(k, v); return \'OK\'; },\n  del: async (k) => store.delete(k),\n  incr: async (k) => { const n = (store.get(k) || 0) + 1; store.set(k, n); return n; },\n};\n```\n\n#### Mongoose / MongoDB (`mongoose`, `mongodb`)\nFind the file calling `mongoose.connect()`. Wrap in try-catch:\n```javascript\nimport mongoose from \'mongoose\';\nmongoose.set(\'bufferCommands\', false); // CRITICAL: fail fast, don\'t hang\nmongoose.connect(process.env.MONGODB_URI || \'mongodb://localhost/mock\')\n  .catch(err => console.warn(\'MongoDB not connected \342\200\224 some features may not work\'));\n\n// CRITICAL route-level fallback: Add Express error middleware in app.js/server.js\n// to handle database queries failing gracefully when MongoDB is offline:\napp.use((err, req, res, next) => {\n  if (err.name === \'MongooseError\' || err.name === \'MongoNetworkError\' || err.message.includes(\'buffering timed out\')) {\n    console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database offline \342\200\224 returning mock empty response\');\n    if (req.method === \'GET\') {\n      // Return empty array/object depending on route path suffix pluralization\n      return res.json(req.path.endsWith(\'s\') || req.path.endsWith(\'s/\') ? [] : {});\n    }\n    return res.status(503).json({ error: \'Service temporarily unavailable (database offline)\' });\n  }\n  next(err);\n});\n```\n\n#### Drizzle ORM (`drizzle-orm`)\nFind the file calling `drizzle()`. Wrap the entire export:\n```typescript\nlet db;\ntry {\n  db = drizzle(/* original connection */);\n} catch {\n  console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database not connected \342\200\224 using mock\');\n  const noOp = { findMany: async () => [], findFirst: async () => null,\n    findUnique: async () => null, create: async (d) => d?.data ?? {},\n    update: async (d) => d?.data ?? {}, delete: async () => ({}) };\n  db = new Proxy({}, {\n    get: (_, prop) => prop === \'query\'\n      ? new Proxy({}, { get: () => noOp }) : async () => [],\n  });\n}\nexport { db };\n```\n\n#### Prisma (`prisma`, `@prisma/client`)\nFind the PrismaClient initialization. Wrap it:\n```typescript\nlet prisma;\ntry {\n  prisma = new PrismaClient();\n} catch {\n  console.warn(\'[AI Studio] Database not connected \342\200\224 using mock\');\n  const noOp = { findMany: async () => [], findFirst: async () => null,\n    findUnique: async () => null, create: async (d) => d?.data ?? {},\n    update: async (d) => d?.data ?? {}, delete: async () => ({}) };\n  prisma = new Proxy({}, { get: () => noOp });\n}\nexport { prisma };\n```\n\n#### PostgreSQL / MySQL raw (`pg`, `postgres`, `mysql2`)\n```javascript\nlet db;\ntry { db = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL }); }\ncatch { console.warn(\'DB not connected \342\200\224 mock active\');\n  db = { query: async () => ({ rows: [] }), connect: async () =>\n    ({ query: async () => ({ rows: [] }), release: () => {} }) }; }\nexport { db };\n```\n\n#### Background Jobs (`bull`, `bullmq`, `kafkajs`, `amqplib`)\nRewrite `queue.add(\'job\', data)` \342\206\222 call the handler function directly inline.\nRemove queue/worker setup. Keep handler functions.\n\n#### SQLite (`sqlite3`, `better-sqlite3`)\nSTRIP native package. Replace with mock:\n```javascript\nexport const db = { prepare: () => ({ get: () => null, all: () => [],\n  run: () => ({ changes: 0 }) }) };\n```\n\n### 2.3 Platform SDKs\n\nScan deps for `@vercel/*`, `@netlify/*`, `@cloudflare/*`:\n\n| Package | Action |\n|---|---|\n| `@vercel/analytics`, `@vercel/speed-insights`, `@vercel/og` | STRIP: remove from deps, replace component with `() => null` |\n| `@netlify/functions`, `@netlify/plugin-*` | STRIP |\n| `@cloudflare/workers-types`, `netlify-identity-widget` | STRIP |\n| `@vercel/kv`, `@vercel/blob`, `@vercel/postgres` | MOCK: replace with in-memory Map stub |\n| `@netlify/blobs` | MOCK: replace with in-memory Map |\n| `@cloudflare/kv-asset-handler` | MOCK: replace with static file serving |\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: Framework Configuration\n\nClassify by deps (first match wins), then apply fixes inline:\n\n### Next.js (`next` in deps)\n- Dev script: `\"dev\": \"next dev -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0\"`\n- Add `output: \'standalone\'` to `next.config.js/ts/mjs`\n- If custom `server.js` exists with `createServer()`: remove it\n  (`standalone` is incompatible with custom servers)\n- Remove `export const runtime = \'edge\'` from any route/middleware\n- Remove Vercel/Cloudflare image loaders from `next/image` config\n\n### Nuxt (`nuxt` in deps)\n- Config: `nitro: { preset: \'node-server\' }`, `devServer: { port: 3000, host: \'0.0.0.0\' }`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"nuxt dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### SvelteKit (`@sveltejs/kit` in deps)\n- SWAP adapter: remove `@sveltejs/adapter-vercel` etc \342\206\222\n  install `@sveltejs/adapter-node`\n- Update `svelte.config.js`: `import adapter from \'@sveltejs/adapter-node\'`\n- **CRITICAL import fix**: search ALL `.svelte` and `.ts` files for\n  `from \'@sveltejs/adapter-vercel\'` and delete those imports \342\200\224 they are\n  type-only adapter config exports that don\'t exist in adapter-node\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vite dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Remix (`@remix-run/*` in deps)\n- Remove `@remix-run/cloudflare`, `@remix-run/vercel`, `@remix-run/deno`\n- Keep/install `@remix-run/node`\n- **CRITICAL import fix**: Replace ALL `from \"@remix-run/cloudflare\"` \342\206\222\n  `from \"@remix-run/node\"` in EVERY route file (`app/routes/`, `app/root.tsx`).\n  Every route typically has this import. Missing even one crashes the build.\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"remix vite:dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Astro (`astro` in deps)\n- SWAP adapter: remove `@astrojs/vercel` etc \342\206\222 install `@astrojs/node`\n- Config: `output: \'server\'`, `adapter: node({ mode: \'standalone\' })`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"astro dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### React SPA (Vite) \342\200\224 `react` in deps, no `next`\n- Vite config: `server: { host: \'0.0.0.0\', port: 3000, allowedHosts: \'all\' }`\n- Or dev script: `\"dev\": \"vite --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### React SPA (CRA) \342\200\224 `react-scripts` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"PORT=3000 HOST=0.0.0.0 react-scripts start\"`\n\n### Angular \342\200\224 `@angular/core` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"ng serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n- If SSR (`@angular/ssr`): ensure `server.ts` binds to `0.0.0.0:3000`\n\n### Vue (plain, no Nuxt) \342\200\224 `vue` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vite --port 3000 --host 0.0.0.0\"`\n\n### SolidStart \342\200\224 `solid-start` in deps\n- Config: `server: { preset: \'node-server\' }`\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"vinxi dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000\"`\n\n### Gatsby \342\200\224 `gatsby` in deps\n- Dev: `\"dev\": \"gatsby develop -p 3000 -H 0.0.0.0\"`\n\n### Node.js Backend Only (Express/Fastify/NestJS/Koa/Hono, no frontend)\n- Rewrite `.listen()` to: `.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')`\n- NestJS: `await app.listen(3000, \'0.0.0.0\')`\n- Fastify: `listen({ port: 3000, host: \'0.0.0.0\' })`\n- Hono: `serve({ fetch: app.fetch, port: 3000, hostname: \'0.0.0.0\' })`\n- If entry is TypeScript: add `tsx` and `\"dev\": \"tsx watch src/index.ts\"`\n- WebSockets on separate port: multiplex over 3000:\n  `const wsServer = new WebSocket.Server({ server: httpServer })`\n\n### SPA + Backend (both frontend and backend in same repo, not monorepo)\nAI Studio runs ONE process via `npm run dev`. Do NOT use `concurrently`.\n- **Preferred**: Build frontend, serve from backend:\n  `\"dev\": \"npm run build:frontend && node server.js\"` + add\n  `app.use(express.static(\'client/dist\'))` AFTER API routes + SPA fallback\n- **Alternative** (if backend has <10 routes): merge API into frontend framework\n\n### Static Site (just HTML, no framework)\n- Find `index.html` in root, `public/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `docs/`\n- Create `server.js` with Express serving the static dir on port 3000\n- `\"dev\": \"node server.js\"`, add `express` to deps\n\n### Unrecognized\n- Try as-is: ensure `dev` script starts on port 3000 (host `0.0.0.0`)\n- Run `install_applet_dependencies` \342\206\222 `compile_applet`\n- Rewrite to supported framework only as last resort\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: Integration Wiring\n\n### Gemini SDK\nIF `@google/generative-ai` or `@google/genai` is in dependencies:\n- Swap `@google/generative-ai` \342\206\222 `@google/genai`\n- Ensure API calls are server-side ONLY\n- Remove hardcoded API keys\n- Add `GEMINI_API_KEY=` to `.env.example`\n\n### Firebase\n- Extract Firebase API key to `.env.example` (FIREBASE_API_KEY=)\n- Ensure no hardcoded production credentials in `initializeApp()` config\n- If `firebase-applet-config.json` exists, use as-is\n\n### Third-party LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.)\n- Ensure API calls are server-side ONLY\n- Add API key variable names to `.env.example`\n\n### Secrets & Env Scan\n1. Scan all source files for `process.env.*` and `import.meta.env.*`\n2. Scan existing .env, .env.local, .env.development for key names\n3. Generate or merge into `.env.example`\n\n\n## Execution Protocol\n\n### Chunked Execution\n\nExecute in discrete chunks. After each phase, yield a status message:\n\n```\n\"\342\234\205 Phase 1 complete. Changes made:\n- Converted from pnpm to npm\n- Detected monorepo \342\200\224 wired root dev script to apps/web (Next.js)\nMoving to dependency validation...\"\n```\n\n### Verification Loop\n\n1. Run `install_applet_dependencies` then `compile_applet`\n2. If errors \342\206\222 read the error, fix the specific issue, retry\n3. Repeat up to 3 times\n\n### Circuit Breaker (HARD STOP)\n\nIf `compile_applet` fails 3 times and you cannot resolve the error: STOP.\nExplain the specific error to the user and ask for help.\n\n### Post-Execution Summary\n\nAfter successful compilation (or circuit breaker), output:\n\n```\n\"\342\234\205 Migration complete! Here\'s what I changed:\n\n**Runtime**: Web (Node.js)\n**Framework**: Detected [framework]\n**Package Manager**: Converted from [original] to npm\n**Dependencies**:\n- [list each mocked/stripped/swapped dependency and why]\n**Config**: [framework-specific changes]\n**Port**: Dev server on port 3000 (0.0.0.0)\n\nTo connect a real database, provision AI Studio Cloud SQL from the\nintegrations menu.\"\n```\n"
    num_lines: 410
    num_bytes: 16203
  }
}
