    prompt_sections {
      title: "skills"
      content: "<skills>\n# Skills\n\nYou can use specialized \'skills\' to help you with tasks. Each skill has a name and a description listed below.\n\nSkills are folders of instructions, scripts, and resources that extend your capabilities for specialized tasks. Each skill folder contains:\n- **SKILL.md** (required): The main instruction file with YAML frontmatter (name, description) and detailed markdown instructions\n\nMore complex skills may include additional directories and files as needed, for example:\n- **references/** - Detailed reference documentation and topic-specific guides\n- **scripts/** - Helper scripts and utilities that extend your capabilities\n- **examples/** - Reference implementations and usage patterns\n- **resources/** - Additional files, templates, or assets the skill may reference\n\nImportant:\n\n- When a skill matches the user\'s request or seems relevant, this is a BLOCKING\n  REQUIREMENT: You MUST use the `view_file` tool on the SKILL.md file to read\n  its full instructions BEFORE generating any other response about the task.\n  Once you have read the instructions, follow them exactly as documented.\n\n\nAvailable skills:\n- applet-seo (/skills/system_skills/applet_seo/SKILL.md): Configures advanced search engine optimization (SEO), OpenGraph social share cards, Twitter cards, and Schema.org structured data (JSON-LD) for web applications in AI Studio. Use when the user requests enhanced SEO, social sharing cards, or rich structured data.\n- cloudsql-execute-sql (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-execute-sql/SKILL.md): Executes SQL statements on the Cloud SQL instance. This tool is designed for data query language (DQL) and data manipulation language (DML) operations, such as querying existing data, seeding databases, and debugging.\n\nDo NOT use this skill for:\n  - Applications that do not use Cloud SQL as their database.\n\nImportant Guidelines:\n  - Do not use this tool for data definition language (DDL) operations (e.g., creating or altering tables); these should be handled by the ORM. Exception: You may use this tool to install PostgreSQL extensions, which the ORM does not support.\n  - Do not use this tool for data control language (DCL) operations.\n  - Do not use this tool to create, update, or delete databases or database users.\n  - Avoid destructive actions like dropping tables or databases.\n  - Use \"sql_statement\" as the argument name. Do not use \"sql\".\n- cloudsql-setup (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-setup/SKILL.md): Provisions a relational Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) database and configures Firebase Authentication together. Do NOT use this skill if only Firebase Authentication is requested without a relational database.\n\nUse this skill ONLY if at least one of the following conditions is met:\n* The user explicitly requests PostgreSQL, SQL, Relational database.\n* The user explicitly requests Cloud SQL, Supabase, Neon, RDS, Aurora.\n\nCapabilities of the provisioned Cloud SQL instance with Developer edition:\n* Near-instant provisioning (~2 seconds).\n* Scale-to-zero capabilities with a free tier for cost savings.\n- cloudsql-update-schema (/skills/system_skills/cloudsql-update-schema/SKILL.md): Updates the Cloud SQL database schema for the app based on the schema defined in src/db/schema.ts and the configuration in src/db/drizzle.config.ts.\nUse this skill if any of the following happen:\n  - The user requests to update their Cloud SQL database schema\n  - Changes are made to the src/db/schema.ts file\n  - Changes are made to the src/db/drizzle.config.ts file\n- firebase-integration (/skills/system_skills/firebase-skill/SKILL.md): Integrates Firebase (Firestore and Auth) into applications, generate secure rules, and handle errors.\n\nUse this skill whenever the application requires:\n* Persistent Data & Database: Storing, querying, and persisting application state, documents, or records across sessions and devices (even if Firebase is not explicitly named).\n* Multi-Role & Access Control (RBAC): Applications with distinct user roles or permissions (e.g., admins, super admins, managers, employees, assignees, creators, customers).\n* User Authentication & Accounts: App user sign-in/login, user profiles, credentials, or private user data.\n* Security Hardening & Rules: Designing schemas, writing/auditing `firestore.rules`, enforcing role validation, or debugging permission errors.\n* SDK & Tool Setup: Provisioning Firebase via `set_up_firebase`, initializing the Firebase SDK in React/TypeScript, or deploying rules via `deploy_firebase`.\n\nDo NOT use this skill for:\n* General GCP resource management outside of the specific Firebase tools provided.\n* Purely transient or single-session apps with no persistence, user accounts, or shared state (e.g., simple unit converters, local calculators).\n* Applications explicitly requesting a relational SQL database like PostgreSQL or Cloud SQL (use cloudsql-setup instead).\n- focus-mode (/skills/system_skills/focus_mode/SKILL.md): Instructions for responding to UI element selection (CSS selectors).\n- gemini-api (/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md): Provides model selection guidance and coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Use when the application requires AI capabilities (e.g., text/image generation, smart features) or when the task involves implementing an \"AI-powered\" feature. The model should prefer this modern SDK over legacy alternatives. Do NOT use for general discussions about AI without implementation intent. Covers model aliases, streaming, chat, function calling, search and maps grounding, Live API, TTS, and API key handling.\n- gemini-interactions-api (/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/SKILL.md): Provides coding patterns for the @google/genai TypeScript SDK. Covers using the Interactions API for the Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, Omni models (Omni Flash), and general model capabilities (text, image, speech generation), as well as other specialized APIs for music (Lyria) and real-time audio (Live API) in a server-side context. Note that Omni models and Agents are only available via the Interactions API, not with standard generateContent. Use when user requests the Interactions API, Antigravity agent, Deep Research agent, or Omni models.\n- github-import-migration (/skills/system_skills/github_import_migration/SKILL.md): Execute-First migration for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio. Triages projects and routes to the appropriate self-contained migration reference. Supports Web (Node.js) and Android (Kotlin/Compose) runtimes.\n- github-import-rewrite (/skills/system_skills/github_import_rewrite/SKILL.md): Cross-framework rewrite for GitHub repositories imported into AI Studio. Rewrites the imported project from its source framework to a different target framework while preserving core features and business logic.\n- google-maps-platform-ghp-integration (/skills/system_skills/google_maps_platform_ghp_integration/SKILL.md): A collection of skills for architecting and implementing production-ready code using Google Maps Platform APIs and SDKs for any map, place, address, geocoding, routing/ETA (including eco-friendly routing), nearby search, 3D / Street View / static map, marker clustering, custom styling, drawing, geofencing, heatmap, or environmental (air-quality / pollen / solar / weather) feature \342\200\224 across Web, Android, iOS, and Web Services APIs. For prototyping, use the public Maps Demo Key \342\200\224 no billing setup and no Cloud project required, covering a growing set of the most popular Google Maps Platform APIs. For production, the skill prompts you to create and restrict your own key. All non-trivial code is grounded in freshly retrieved docs via the Google Maps Platform Code Assist service (no reliance on training-data memory).\n- image-generation (/skills/system_skills/image_generation/SKILL.md): Use when the application needs to generate or update images \342\200\224 hero banners, illustrations, icons, backgrounds, avatars, product photos, or any visual asset. Covers image selection strategy (using tools vs assets vs placeholders) and runtime generation using Gemini models.\n- oauth-integration (/skills/system_skills/oauth/SKILL.md): Guidelines for implementing Third-Party (3P) OAuth flows with external non-Google services (e.g., GitHub, Discord, Strava, Spotify, Slack, etc.) in the AI Studio preview environment. Use when the user requests third-party OAuth, login with external services, or popup-based authentication. Covers iframe constraints, cookie configuration, and redirect URI setup.\n- pwa-integration (/skills/system_skills/pwa_integration/SKILL.md): Step-by-step instructions for building a new Progressive Web App (PWA) or integrating PWA compliance into a web application (Vite or Next.js) with offline capabilities, service workers, Web App Manifests, icon assets, and in-app install prompts. Use when building a new PWA or adding PWA support, offline capabilities, or installability to a web app.\n- real-time-and-multi-user (/skills/system_skills/realtime_guidelines/SKILL.md): Guidelines for implementing real-time features, WebSockets, and collaborative canvases. Use when the app requires chat, live collaboration, multiplayer games, or notifications. Covers server-authoritative state, event-based communication, and canvas library selection (Konva, Fabric.js).\n- shadcn-ui (/skills/system_skills/shadcn/SKILL.md): Guidelines for using shadcn/ui components and CLI. Use ONLY when the user requests shadcn or shadcn/ui. Covers initialization, adding components, community registries, and theming.\n- workspace-integration (/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md): Integrate 1P Google Workspace APIs (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Calendar, Gmail, Chat, Meet, Forms, Classroom, Tasks, Keep, People, Picker) into the application. Use when the user wants to authenticate with Google Workspace to read, write, or search Google Workspace data. Requires OAuth configuration via the set_up_oauth and remove_oauth tools.\n\n</skills>"
